Z||000000||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-09-2000||09:03 PM||||Ok this is the last question I will ask about engine swaps.  I need to know if I go with the 3.1 or the 3.4 motor(engine) what do I use from my 2.8 and what would I have to get?  If I do go with the 3.1 or 3.4 is there any special codes that I should look for to get the higher Horse power motor?  Also is it better to go and buy a reman motor or go to a junkyard and get one and rebuild it?  Thanks for all you help.  You guys have been great.<P>Later,<BR>Jack||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-10-2000||04:53 PM||||If you are going to spend that king of money..... have you looked at the GM crate motors? Those come pretty much any way you want them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||08-10-2000||08:26 PM||||You should get a low mileage Camaro 3.4 with the injectors so that all you have to do is bolt it in and go. The biggest hurtle is drilling the starter bolts and modifying the front engine mount. George Miller from the Fiero Shop should be able to help you out with the starter relocation. Ed Parks from the Fiero Factory should be able to get you a modified engine mount and AC bracket. There is a check valve in the oil passage of your 2.8 that you need to transplant in the 3.4 also. It’s easy because I am in the middle of this transplant right now and I have already drilled the starter holes and modified the mounts. The whole swap cost me less than $1000 and I will have about 180 HP and buckets of low-end torque. I got the motor from a 93 Firebird with 51,000 miles on it. <P>About the codes I don’t know about the 3.1 engine but the 3.4 pushrod Camaro ( F-Body) engines are all the same (93-95). You are better off with going with more displacement. A Stock Camaro engine in a fiero will accelerate it from 0-60 mph in 6.2 seconds and run the quarter in the high fourteens. Modify it with headers, a performance three angle valve job (done right), a good exhaust, and a 50 hp shot of Nitrous and you will have a rocket ship.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||1
